{"name":"Brick Hearth","hex":"#956159","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"brick","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A hardened rectangular block of mud, clay etc., used for building.","Such hardened mud, clay, etc. considered collectively, as a building material."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To build, line, or form with bricks.","To make into bricks."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brick"},{"term":"hearth","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The place in a home where a fire is or was traditionally kept for home heating and for cooking, usually constituted by at least a hearthstone and often enclosed to varying degrees by any combination of reredos, fireplace, oven, smoke hood, or chimney.","A hearthstone, either as standalone or as the floor of an enclosed fireplace or oven."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hearth"}],"entries":[{"title":"Brick","blocks":[{"text":"A brick is a type of building material used to build walls, pavements, and other elements in masonry construction. Properly, the term brick denotes a unit primarily composed of clay, but it is now also used informally to denote building units made of other materials or other chemically cured construction blocks."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Brick.jpg/330px-Brick.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brick","wikidata":"Q40089"},{"title":"Hearth","blocks":[{"text":"A hearth is the place in a home where a fire is or was traditionally kept for home heating and for cooking, usually constituted by a horizontal hearthstone and often enclosed to varying degrees by any combination of reredos, fireplace, oven, smoke hood, or chimney. Hearths are usually composed of masonry such as brick or stone. For millennia, the hearth was such an integral part of a home, usually its central and most important feature, that the concept has been generalized to refer to a homeplace or household, as in the terms \"hearth and home\" and \"keep the home fires burning\". In the modern era, since the advent of central heating, hearths are usually less central to most people's daily life because the heating of the home is instead done by a furnace or a heating stove, and cooking is instead done with a kitchen stove/range alongside other home appliances; thus many homes built in the 20th and 21st centuries do not have hearths. Nonetheless, many homes still have hearths, which still help serve the purposes of warmth, cooking, and comfort."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/RFK-005-Feuerstelle-im-17-Jh.JPG/330px-RFK-005-Feuerstelle-im-17-Jh.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hearth","wikidata":"Q585473"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Brick_wall_close-up_view.jpg/500px-Brick_wall_close-up_view.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Brick_wall_close-up_view.jpg/1280px-Brick_wall_close-up_view.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Brick_wall_close-up_view.jpg/500px-Brick_wall_close-up_view.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A wall constructed in glazed-headed Flemish bond brickwork pattern, with various shades and lengths","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABrick_wall_close-up_view.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/%D9%86%D9%85%D8%A7%DB%8C_4.jpg/500px-%D9%86%D9%85%D8%A7%DB%8C_4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/%D9%86%D9%85%D8%A7%DB%8C_4.jpg/1280px-%D9%86%D9%85%D8%A7